# ==============================================================================
# CODEOWNERS — who must review what
#
# Docs: MAINTAINERS.md (the same information in words) · GOVERNANCE.md
#
# A pull request that touches a path listed here cannot merge until one of the
# path's owners approves it ("Protect main" requires a code-owner review).
#
# HOW TO READ THIS FILE
#   * The LAST matching pattern wins, so `*` comes first.
#   * Owners are the organisation's teams wherever a team matches the
#     responsibility; individuals only where no team does (club leadership
#     documents).
#
# WHY TEAMS
#   Listing every maintainer by name made GitHub request a review from all
#   seven of them on every pull request, so nobody in particular owned it.
#   A team is requested once. With "Code review assignment" turned on in the
#   team's settings (Organisation → Teams → <team> → Settings → Code review),
#   GitHub assigns one or two members in rotation instead — see MAINTAINERS.md.
#
# A team named here must exist and have write access to this repository, or the
# entry matches nothing and, with code-owner review required, nothing under it
# could ever merge. `gh api repos/Open-Source-Software-Club/OSS_website/codeowners/errors`
# lists any line GitHub cannot resolve.
#
# TEAMS (membership is managed in the organisation settings)
#   @Open-Source-Software-Club/technical-leads — CI/CD, security, database
#   @Open-Source-Software-Club/core-team       — everything else
# ==============================================================================

# Default owner for everything in the repository.
*                                   @Open-Source-Software-Club/core-team

